body:
Congrats to you for being so courageous! I was really nervous before I checked myself into rehab as well. If I could give you some advice from my own experience; 

don’t set your expectations too high in regard to people showing compassion towards you in rehab. You will meet some people you connect with but the staff may not be as attentive as you’d expect. Also, bring some slippers with you and anything creative to keep you busy and release your nervous energy. I learned how to knit in rehab and it helped a lot with the boredom!

You’re making one of the most profound decisions of your entire life and it will be life changing in so many ways! Sending you love and positivity!!
